==German==

===Etymology===
{{af|de|sauer|Stoff}}, {{calque|de|fr|oxygène|nocap=1}}, from Greek-Latin {{m|la|oxygenium||acid-maker}}, due to a mistaken early belief that oxygen was a necessary ingredient in all acids.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈzaʊ̯ɐʃtɔf/}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-Sauerstoff.ogg|Audio (Austria)}}
* {{audio|de|De-Sauerstoff.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Sauerstoffs|-|gen2=Sauerstoffes}}

# [[oxygen]]
#: {{uxi|de|'''Sauerstoff''' [[tanken]]|to breathe fresh air (literally "to fill up on oxygen" like fuel)}}
